{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>רב</b> — from רבי המלך, meaning that the great and eminent one of the nation is the one who carries out everything, and rules, and gives wages to the fool and compels him in his labor; and likewise hires עוברים — these are the refractory ones, as in מדוע אתה עובר. Another interpretation: this verse is joined to the one above." "And the word רב — [means] much, as in רב לכם. And so the interpretation: the ruling fool employs many; he makes everyone like a thorn in the hand of a drunkard. And whoever hires the fool and gives wages to עוברים performs a commandment he is unable to enforce — and so they transgressed and were punished."], :book :proverbs, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 26, :notes {0 "The phrase רבי המלך (rendered 'great/eminent one of the king') may be an epithet or citation; its precise referent is uncertain.", 1 "The syntax of עובד מצות שאין יכולת להכריחם is compressed and slightly obscure; rendered hyper-literally."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Proverbs -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/mishley/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:24:52.312794196Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}